{
  "query": "You are the Cloud Database Engineer for BlueOrbit Media, a multinational streaming platform. The leadership team requires a fully managed relational database that can scale globally with low latency, and a separate set of legacy applications must continue running on dedicated physical servers hosted in Google Cloud for compliance. Which Google Cloud services and configuration would satisfy both the managed database and the bare metal workload requirements?",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Use Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL for the managed database service and Anthos on bare metal for the bare metal infrastructure",
      "explanation": "Cloud SQL offers a managed PostgreSQL service while Anthos on bare metal runs Kubernetes clusters on customer provided physical servers",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Use Cloud Spanner for the managed database service and Bare Metal Solution for the bare metal infrastructure",
      "explanation": "Cloud Spanner is a fully managed relational database with global scalability and Bare Metal Solution provides dedicated physical servers in Google data centers",
      "correct": true,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Use Cloud Bigtable for the managed database service and Google Kubernetes Engine with node pools of bare metal machines for the bare metal infrastructure",
      "explanation": "Cloud Bigtable is a managed wide column NoSQL database and Google Kubernetes Engine manages containerized workloads on Compute Engine nodes",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Use Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL for the managed database service and Google Compute Engine with sole-tenant nodes for the bare metal infrastructure",
      "explanation": "Cloud SQL provides managed PostgreSQL instances and sole-tenant nodes place your virtual machines on dedicated host hardware",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    }
  ],
  "answer": "<p>The correct choice is <b>Use Cloud Spanner for the managed database service and Bare Metal Solution for the bare metal infrastructure</b>. <b>Cloud Spanner</b> delivers a fully managed relational database that scales globally with high availability and low latency. <b>Bare Metal Solution</b> provides dedicated physical servers hosted in Google Cloud to keep legacy workloads compliant while remaining connected to native services.</p><p>With <b>Cloud Spanner</b> you get a globally distributed relational store with automatic synchronous replication across regions and strong consistency. It supports horizontal scaling without downtime and is designed for low latency reads and writes across the world.</p><p><b>Bare Metal Solution</b> supplies single tenant physical servers in Google Cloud facilities and offers direct low latency connectivity to Google Cloud networks. It is intended for specialized or licensed software and strict compliance needs that cannot run on virtualized compute.</p><p><i>Use Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL for the managed database service and Anthos on bare metal for the bare metal infrastructure</i> is not suitable because Cloud SQL is regional and does not provide a globally distributed relational database with low latency at planetary scale. Anthos on bare metal targets customer operated on premises hardware rather than dedicated physical servers hosted by Google Cloud.</p><p><i>Use Cloud Bigtable for the managed database service and Google Kubernetes Engine with node pools of bare metal machines for the bare metal infrastructure</i> is incorrect because Cloud Bigtable is a NoSQL wide column database rather than a relational service. In Google Cloud the nodes in Google Kubernetes Engine are Compute Engine virtual machines and there is no bare metal node pool offering.</p><p><i>Use Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL for the managed database service and Google Compute Engine with sole-tenant nodes for the bare metal infrastructure</i> does not meet the requirements because Cloud SQL is not a globally scalable relational service. Sole tenant nodes provide dedicated hosts for virtual machines and they are not bare metal.</p>",
